---
import Legal from "../layouts/Legal.astro";
import { LEGAL } from "../legal";

const sections = [
  { id: "summary", title: "The short version" },
  { id: "website", title: "This website" },
  { id: "app", title: "The Mates app" },
  { id: "use", title: "How we use it" },
  { id: "sharing", title: "Who we share it with" },
  { id: "retention", title: "How long we keep it" },
  { id: "rights", title: "Your rights" },
  { id: "security", title: "Security" },
  { id: "children", title: "Children" },
  { id: "changes", title: "Changes" },
  { id: "contact", title: "Contact" },
];
const mail = `mailto:${LEGAL.contact}`;
---

<Legal title="Privacy Policy" description="What Mates collects, why, who it is shared with, and how to get it deleted." sections={sections}>
  <h2 id="summary">The short version</h2>
  <p class="summary">
    We collect what Mates needs to work for you and nothing more. We don’t sell your data or use it for advertising. The
    website sets no cookies. You can delete your account, and everything in it, at any time.
  </p>
  <p>
    This policy explains how {LEGAL.operator} (“we”, “us”), who operates {LEGAL.product}, handles personal information on
    {LEGAL.site} and in the {LEGAL.product} mobile app. It applies wherever you are, and we follow Ghana’s Data Protection
    Act, 2012 (Act 843) and, where they apply to you, laws such as the EU and UK GDPR.
  </p>

  <h2 id="website">This website</h2>
  <h3>The waitlist</h3>
  <p>
    If you join the waitlist we store your email address, the time you joined, and the site that sent you to us (for
    example “x.com”), if any. We use your email only to tell you when {LEGAL.product} is ready.
  </p>
  <h3>Visit counts</h3>
  <p>
    To count visits we record, for each page view, the page, the time, the referring site’s name, and whether you used a
    phone, tablet or computer. To count unique visitors without tracking you, we turn your IP address and browser details
    into a one-way code that changes every day. We never store your IP address, and the code can’t be traced back to you
    or linked across days. Crawlers and link previews are not counted.
  </p>
  <p>The website sets no cookies and uses no advertising or third-party tracking scripts.</p>

  <h2 id="app">The Mates app</h2>
  <h3>Your account</h3>
  <p>Your name, email address and profile picture, from your sign-up or from Apple or Google if you sign in with them.</p>
  <h3>What you give your mates</h3>
  <p>
    Your messages, the photos and files you share, the mates and groups you create, missions, notes, routines and the
    results your mates produce. This is the content Mates needs to do the work you ask for.
  </p>
  <h3>Apps you connect</h3>
  <p>
    When you connect an app such as Gmail or Google Calendar, your mates can read and act in it on your instructions. The
    sign-in for those apps is held by our connections provider, not stored by us. You can disconnect any app at any time.
  </p>
  <h3>GitHub</h3>
  <p>
    If you install the Mates GitHub app, we store which accounts and repositories you gave it. When a mate works on your
    code, it copies the repository to a private, temporary computer that is deleted when the run ends. Changes come back
    as a pull request; the mates never merge.
  </p>
  <h3>Device and usage</h3>
  <p>
    A push notification token, so we can tell you when work is done, and basic technical logs (such as errors and request
    times) to keep the service running.
  </p>

  <h2 id="use">How we use it</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>To run {LEGAL.product}: answer your messages, carry out the tasks you give your mates, and keep your history.</li>
    <li>To send you notifications you asked for, and, if you joined the waitlist, the launch email.</li>
    <li>To keep the service secure, prevent abuse, and fix problems.</li>
    <li>To understand, in aggregate, how the website and app are used, so we can improve them.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    We process your information to provide the service you signed up for, with your consent (such as the waitlist and
    connected apps, which you can withdraw), and for our legitimate interest in keeping {LEGAL.product} safe and working.
    We don’t train our own AI models on your content, and we don’t sell or rent personal information. The AI providers
    listed below handle the messages they process under their own data policies.
  </p>

  <h2 id="sharing">Who we share it with</h2>
  <p>
    {LEGAL.product} is built on trusted providers who process data for us, only to run the service. Depending on what you
    use, they include:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li><b>Clerk</b>, for sign-in and accounts.</li>
    <li><b>Neon</b>, our database, which holds your account, chats and files.</li>
    <li><b>Railway</b> and <b>Vercel</b>, which host our servers and this website.</li>
    <li><b>OpenRouter</b> and the AI model providers it routes to, which process your messages to generate replies.</li>
    <li><b>Composio</b>, which manages the apps you connect.</li>
    <li><b>Browserbase</b>, which runs a cloud browser when a mate needs to use a website for you.</li>
    <li><b>GitHub</b> and <b>Modal</b>, for coding tasks on your repositories and the temporary computers they run on.</li>
    <li><b>Trigger.dev</b>, which runs long tasks in the background.</li>
    <li><b>Expo</b>, which delivers push notifications.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    These providers may store or process data outside your country. We only share information when the law requires it
    or to protect people’s safety, and otherwise never with anyone else.
  </p>

  <h2 id="retention">How long we keep it</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Account data and your content: until you delete it or delete your account.</li>
    <li>Waitlist emails: until we’ve sent the launch email, or sooner if you ask us to remove you.</li>
    <li>Visit counts: these hold nothing that identifies you, and we keep them to see trends over time.</li>
    <li>Coding computers: deleted when each run ends.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>Deleting your account in Settings removes your data from our systems and disconnects your apps and GitHub.</p>

  <h2 id="rights">Your rights</h2>
  <p>
    You can ask to see, correct, export or delete your personal information, and object to or limit how we use it. Most of
    this you can do yourself in the app. For anything else, email <a href={mail}>{LEGAL.contact}</a> and we’ll reply within
    30 days. You can also complain to your local data protection authority; in Ghana, that’s the Data Protection
    Commission.
  </p>

  <h2 id="security">Security</h2>
  <p>
    Data is encrypted in transit, access is limited to what each part of the service needs, and coding work runs on
    isolated computers with short-lived, single-repository access. No system is perfectly secure, but we work to protect
    your information and will tell you promptly if a breach affects you.
  </p>

  <h2 id="children">Children</h2>
  <p>
    {LEGAL.product} is not meant for anyone under 13, or the minimum age to consent in your country if higher. We don’t
    knowingly collect their information; if you believe a child has used {LEGAL.product}, contact us and we’ll delete it.
  </p>

  <h2 id="changes">Changes</h2>
  <p>
    If we change this policy we’ll update the date at the top, and for significant changes we’ll tell you in the app or by
    email before they take effect.
  </p>

  <h2 id="contact">Contact</h2>
  <p>
    Questions or requests about your privacy: <a href={mail}>{LEGAL.contact}</a>. {LEGAL.product} is operated by
    {LEGAL.operator}, {LEGAL.country}.
  </p>
</Legal>
